S WindowExchange.h | 34 lines | ff830e25 | 2 sym | Native window handle ⇄ VkSurfaceKHR — the one place the window system meets the vendor edge.

//------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//                                                     THE CONVERSION
//------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

F Convert | WindowExchange.h | 27 | api,nonthrowing | 🚩 | Converts a native window handle from `04` into a presentation surface. The split is what keeps `SlateMath` free of a Vulkan header.
    in    Instance      VkInstance  [-]  the instance the surface is created against
    in    NativeHandle  void*       [-]  the opaque handle `WindowInterchange` surrendered; never a GLFW spelling above
    out   -             Deliver     [-]  refuses with HostDenied when the window system declines the surface
    by    Source/WindowExchange.cpp, Source/WorkspaceSequence.cpp
    note  ⚠️ `WindowInterchange` in `SlateMath` and `WindowExchange` here are distinct and both required.

F Reclaim | WindowExchange.h | 32 | api,nonthrowing | ✔️ | Destroys a surface previously converted.
    in    Instance             VkInstance    [-]  ?
    in    PresentationSurface  VkSurfaceKHR  [-]  ?
    out   -                    void          [-]  ?
    by    Api/AttachmentIndex.h, Api/ByteSpace.h, Api/CodeInterchange.h, Api/CommandSequence.h, Api/CycleScheduler.h, Api/DepthReduction.h, (+79 more)
